# apocalypse-won-chat.vrs: D26's won announcement on its own (Session 1 run 8 read the won log and scoreboard but its chat
# OCR missed the line). apo-test with one horde: Chaos at hotspot 1 holds horde 1 at its origin (the fixture goal is 200 m
# away, past the 90 m margin), kills it, and the chat shows "the living have won" at once. hordes.count goes back to 2.
# Needs: apocalypse.vrs's setup (apo-test in events.json, fixture goal); no purge cooldown (wait 240 s after a purge).
# Run: --var H1X=-1360 --var H1Z=-1354
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event set apo-test action.hordes.count 1
expect-reply apo-test action.hordes.count =
chat .devtp ${H1X} ${H1Z}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 1/1 rose at hotspot 1: 8 units timeout=90
wait 5
chat .devkill -1967480038 400
chat .devkill -1618703048 400
wait 5
chat .devkill -1967480038 400
chat .devkill -1618703048 400
expect-log event apo-test ended: won \(1 of 1 hordes risen\) timeout=60
expect-chat the living have won timeout=20
shot chat apo-won-chat
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
chat .nyar event set apo-test action.hordes.count 2
expect-reply apo-test action.hordes.count =
console TPHome
